  "findings": [
    "The candidate sends no session status request. The baseline sends one per wallet.",
    "In the candidate the wallet startup reaches the Router 540 to 615 ms before respond arrives. In the baseline it arrives 280 to 469 ms after.",
    "Starting the objects earlier shortened no later request. In both arms every role request in the Yao stage spent 245 to 540 ms outside its object.",
    "After the Yao stage, a consume, sign prepare, or sign request spends either 9 to 32 ms outside its object or 378 to 536 ms. Two of nine waited in the baseline and seven of nine in the candidate.",
    "Those waits add 0, 492, and 525 ms per baseline wallet and 378, 1251, and 1441 ms per candidate wallet. They exceed the difference between the arms.",
    "No end-to-end gain is measured."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three samples per arm. No control arm, so drift between arms is not measured.",
    "Whether a request waits for its object varies per request. This run cannot tell chance from an effect of the candidate.",
    "The trace arm did not run, so D1 and service round trips per request are not measured on staging.",
    "Worker wall time minus object wall time includes the Worker's own work. Fast calls bound that work at about 30 ms for consume and signing.",
    "Fresh wallets do not prove cold Workers. Worker cold starts were not controlled."
  ],
